commit: e8730f8041bfd42da33e09f422c0e94378430a06
why vendored: upstream imports MulticoreTSNE at load time; its PyPI sdist no
  longer builds and conda-forge's multicore-tsne is py310-only with a version
  string pixi cannot parse. Only randomly.py is used; tSNE plotting is not.
patches (marked VENDORED-PATCH):
  - the MulticoreTSNE and seaborn imports are optional; both are only used by
    plotting helpers the module never calls.
  - _fit: the per-component noise max is hoisted out of its loop, the cleaned X
    is Vs (Vs^T X) instead of (Vs Vs^T) X, and the Wisharts and the shuffled copy
    are freed once decomposed. 10k cells: 956 s -> 167 s, 12.5 -> 9.0 GB.
    tests/vendor_patch.py checks Rm's results against the verbatim code.
